# Untitled

Thermocatalytic Conversion of \(\mathbf{CO}_{2}\) to Valuable Products Activated by Noble-Metal-Free Metal-Organic Frameworks
## 1. Introduction
Carbon dioxide \(\left(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\right)\) plays an important role in the global carbon cycle, and also participates in maintaining the carbon balance in the ecological environment. With the speeding up of industrialization, the high demand for energy and chemicals has increased the concentration of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) in the atmosphere. A very recent report by the Mauna Loa Observatory in Hawaii revealed that the atmospheric concentration of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) is about \(418\,\mathrm{ppm}\), approximately \(50\,\%\) higher than pre-industrial concentrations.[1] The increasing \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) emission has caused many environmental and climatic
