## 2.1. Cycloaddition of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) and Aziridines
Cu based catalysts usually has high efficiency for cycloaddition of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) and aziridines. Hence, Zhao and co-workers synthesized a Cu MOF with \(\left[\mathrm{Cu}_{30}\right]\) nanocages (Figure 3a–c),[85] this MOF can serve as heterogeneous catalyst in \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) conversion with aziridines in a solvent-free system, and the yield of product oxazolidinones can reach \(99\,\%\) under \(2\,\mathrm{MPa}\) of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) in \(12\,\mathrm{h}\). In addition, this catalyst can be reused at least 10 times without any obvious loss in catalytic activity. In 2018, Ma and co-workers synthesized a new Cu-MOF (MMPF-10) based on an octatopic porphyrin ligand,[86] which possesses two unique accessible \(\mathrm{Cu}^{\mathrm{II}}\) centers and a large channel with cross-sectional dimensions of \(25.6\times\) \(15.6\,\mathrm{\AA}\). The calculated free space is \(79.6\,\%\) based on PLATON, and the Brunauer–Emmett–Teller (BET) surface area of \(\approx419\,\mathrm{m}^{2}\,\mathrm{g}^{-1}\). Owing to the porous structure and Lewis acid sites, MMPF-10 shows a high catalytic activity in cycloaddition of aziridines with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\), and the yield of oxazolidinones can reach \(99\,\%\) under \(2\,\mathrm{MPa}\) of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) with tetrabutylammonium bromide (TBAB) as co-catalyst. Subsequently, Zhao and co-workers obtained a stable Ni-MOF with a large Langmuir surface area of \(3789\,\mathrm{m}^{2}\,\mathrm{g}^{-1}\),[87] which exhibits a high \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) adsorption capacity of \(104.0\,\mathrm{cm}^{3}\,\mathrm{g}^{-1}\) at \(273\,\mathrm{K}\). Owing to the Lewis-base sites in MOF structure, this Ni-MOF even can catalyze the cycloaddition of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) and aziridines in the absence of co-catalyst, which is rather rare reported in MOF catalysts. In addition, this catalyst can be reused at least five times, and also has high catalytic activity for the gram-scale experiment. The mechanism was also proposed based on control experiments and characterization results: First, MOF can activate the aziridine substrate and adsorb \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) during catalytic reaction, which will shorten the contact distance between \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) and aziridines. Second, an intermediate is formed through the interaction between the \(\mathrm{N}\) atom of aziridines and the \(\mathrm{C}\) atom of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\). Finally, the product oxazolidinones is obtained through simultaneous three-membered ring-open and five-membered ring-closure.
Metal nodes and functional organic linkers are the catalytic centers in pristine MOFs, which can act as Lewis acid/base sites to activate \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) or substrates. Hence, efficient catalysts can be constructed through rationally regulating metal ions or organic linkers. Recently, Zhao's group synthesized a \(\left[\mathrm{Co}_{3}\right]\) clusters-based MOF by BTB (BTB = 1,3,5-tri(4-carboxyphenyl)benzene) ligands (Figure 4),[88] which exhibited a good efficiency for cycloaddition of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) and aziridines because of its abundant open metal sites. However, it showed a low activity for carboxylation cyclization of propargyl amines and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) due to the lack of Lewis base sites. Interestingly, the types of catalytic centers were regulated after introducing nitrogen-containing ligand XN into framework as Lewis base sites to coordinate with a part of open metal sites, resulting in the performance of the obtained catalyst was opposite to that of original catalyst. Namely, the catalytic yield for carboxylation cyclization of
\(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) with propargyl amines is significantly improved by introducing Lewis base sites, but the yield for cycloaddition of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) with aziridines is much lower than that of the original catalyst with abundant Lewis acid sites. This work indicates that the catalytic activity of MOFs can turn on/off in different reactions.
## 2.2. Carboxylation Cyclization of Propargyl Amines and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\)
Cycloaddition of aziridines with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) is a useful method to produce oxazolidinones, but synthesis of substrate aziridines is used toxic bromine. In addition, aziridines is unstable in air, which is easily oxidized or hydrolyzed after exposing in humid or oxygenated environment.[9] Carboxylation cyclization of propargyl amines and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) is another promising way to synthesis of oxazolidinones, because the substrate propargyl amines is commercially available. In addition, the product oxazolidinones obtained from propargyl amines has a methylene group, which can be used to perform polymerization reactions or post-modification.[90] However, carboxylation cyclization of propargyl amines and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) often needs novel catalysts to activate, such as \(\mathrm{Ag}\) ion, because its versatile coordination geometries and its soft \(\pi\)-Lewis acid in catalytic reactions. For example, Duan's group synthesized two silver-cluster-based MOFs by incorporating thiourea on the backbone of the tripodal ligands,[91] which have abundant active sites and large pores. These MOFs can serve as high-efficiency \(\pi\)-activation catalysts in carboxylation cyclization of propargylamines with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) at atmospheric pressure and room temperature. Both of them have higher activity and reusability than that of other standard silver catalysts. Fei's group synthesized an alkaline-resistant \(\mathrm{Ag}^{\mathrm{I}}\)-anchored MOF through postsynthetic modification of pyrazolate-based linkers,[92] this noble containing MOF exhibits a \(99\,\%\) yield of product in carboxylation cyclization of propargyl amines, which is much higher than that of original MOF without modification. Sun and co-workers constructed a silver cluster-based MOF \(\left(\mathrm{Ag}_{27}\mathrm{-MOF}\right)\),[93] which presents a cationic
2D framework based on the saddle-shaped 27-nuclear silver(I) clusters and porphyrin ligands. \(\mathrm{Ag}_{27}\mathrm{-MOF}\) can catalyze carboxylation cyclization of propargylamines with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) under mild condition, and the turnover number can reach 1333. The density function theory (DFT) calculations suggest that the substrate can easily bind to the exposed \(\mathrm{Ag}\) atoms in the 2D framework through \(\pi\)-interactions of \(\mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{C}\) bonds, which enable \(\mathrm{Ag}_{27}\mathrm{-MOF}\) exhibit an excellent catalytic performance in carboxylation cyclization of propargylamines with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\).
In order to meet the industrial demand, noble-metal-free catalysts are highly desired, and many scientists have devoted a great effort for this research. Amines can react with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) to form a reversible covalent \(\mathrm{C}-\mathrm{N}\) bond via nucleophilic attack, hence it can be introduced in MOFs for \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) capture and activation to increase the catalytic reaction rate. Hence, Sun and co-workers synthesized a Cd-MOF with un-coordinated \(\mathrm{NH}_{2}\) groups in the framework.[94] This MOF catalyst exhibits unprecedented activity and broad substrate scope for the carboxylation cyclization of propargyl amines and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\), and the turnover number (TON) can reach 9300 under \(0.5\,\mathrm{MPa}\) of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) and \(60\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\). Zhao and coworkers synthesized a \(\mathrm{Zn}\) based MOF with \(\left[\mathrm{Zn}_{14}\right]\) and \(\left[\mathrm{Zn}_{4}\right]\) nodes assembled from giant \(\left[\mathrm{Zn}_{116}\right]\) nanocages (Figure 5a–d),[95] which exhibits promising application in efficiently and circularly catalyzing carboxylation cyclization of propargylic amines with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) to afford 2-oxazolidinones under mild conditions. This catalyst can be reused at least ten times
without any obvious decrease in catalytic efficiency, suggesting that this noble-metal-free catalyst has an excellent recyclability. DFT calculations combined with Nuclear Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopy (NMR) and FT-IR spectroscopy results reveal that zinc clusters play an important role in activating \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) and \(\mathrm{C/C}\) bonds of propargylic amines.
Utilization of flue gas as \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) source is a promising strategy to synthesize oxazolidinones, because it can reduce the cost of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) storage and transportation in industry. However, the low concentration of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) will limit the yield of product. Hence, Zhao and co-workers designed a \(\mathrm{Cu^{I}/Cu^{II}}\) mixed valence MOF catalyst by ligand 5-aminonicotinic acid (Figure 5e–g),[94] which contains \(\left[\mathrm{Cu}_{4}\mathrm{I}_{5}\right]\) clusters and \(\left[\mathrm{Cu}_{2}\right]\) paddle wheel nodes. This MOF has a 1D channel with a size of \(1.45\;\mathrm{nm}\), and uncoordinated -NH2 groups and open metal sites are distributed around the channel. Owing to the synergetic effect between \(\mathrm{Cu^{II}}\) ion and \(\mathrm{Cu^{I}}\) ion, this catalyst not only can efficiently catalyze the carboxylation cyclization of propargylamine into oxazolidinones under co-catalyst free and solvent-free conditions, but also can directly utilize \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) in flue gas as raw materials to perform this reaction under green conditions. After comparing the catalytic effect of -OH and - \(\mathrm{NH}_{2}\) groups in the framework. They also found that the anchored \(-\mathrm{NH}_{2}\) groups can improve the catalytic efficiency of MOF catalyst for the carboxylation cyclization of propargylamine with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\). The possible mechanism for this reaction was proposed based on in situ Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FT-IR) spectra and nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) results. 1) The \(-\mathrm{NH}_{2}\) groups can serve as a Lewis-base site to assist dehydrogenation of propargylamines. 2) The activated nitrogen atom of the propargylamines reacts with carbon dioxide to form a carbamate anion. 3) The \(\mathrm{C}{\equiv}\mathrm{C}\) bond of propargylamines is activated by \(\mathrm{Cu^{I}}\) sites in MOF, and the carbamate ion transition state is formed. 4) A five-membered ring is formed by intramolecular ring closure reaction. 5) The target product is obtained through hydrogen transfer, and the catalyst is regenerated at the same time. More recently, Duan's group synthesized a Cu based framework Cu-TSP by a tripod ligand containing thiourea groups (Figure 5h),[97] which can act as a \(\pi\) -activated catalyst to effectively catalyze the cyclization of propargylic amines with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) into 2-oxazolidinones by using DBU as the base under ambient conditions.
## 2.3. Synthesis of Oxazolidinones by Three-Components Reaction
Three component reaction of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) is another promising way to synthesis of oxazolidinones, which because the substrate is cheap and easily obtained, and the functional groups in product is flexible.[98] However, due to the complex reaction procedure, such three-components reaction was mainly performed by noble-metal catalysts, and the by-products are often inevitably mixed in products. For example, organosulfonate-based MOFs have high polar porosity and inherent metal/linker vacancies, these advantages enable them widely applied as catalysts or carrier in many reactions.
Hence, Fei's group utilized a mixed-linker strategy to construct 3D organosulfonate-based MOFs,[99] and TMOF-3 was obtained by reaction of Cu salts with 1,2,4,5-benzenetetramethanesulfonate and \(4{,}4^{\prime}\) -bipyridine. Unfortunately, this Cu MOF exhibits a poor activity for three-component carboxylic cyclization of propargyl alcohol, \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\), and primary amine in one pot to synthesis of oxazolidinones. After introducing \(\mathrm{Ag^{I}}\) sites in the sulfonate sites of TMOF-3 through impregnation method, the \(\mathrm{Ag^{I}}\) -decorated TMOF-3 exhibits high catalytic activity for this reaction, suggesting that sulfonate-based MOFs with high-polarity pore surfaces have potential applications in \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) capture and conversion.
In 2021, Helal and co-workers synthesized a Ni-MOF which is iso-structural to the HKUST-1.[1,66] The \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) uptake of this Ni-MOF is \(37\;\mathrm{cm}^{3}\,\mathrm{g}^{-1}\) at \(273\;\mathrm{K}\) and \(23\;\mathrm{cm}^{3}\,\mathrm{g}^{-1}\) at \(298\;\mathrm{K}\), and its \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) adsorption enthalpy is calculated to be \(20.1\;\mathrm{kJ}\,\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\). As a heterogeneous catalyst, this Ni-MOF can catalyze three component reaction of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\), epoxides and aromatic amines to synthesis of oxazolidinones in \(85\,\%\) yield at \(0.1\;\mathrm{MPa}\) \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) and \(90\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\). They proved that the Lewis acid sites \(\mathrm{Ni^{II}}\) ions are the active sites and TBAI is the co-catalyst.
Synthesis of oxazolidinones using MOF catalysts have presented many impressive achievements, but the corresponding studies about noble-metal-free catalysts are still in its infancy.[101] Especially, the substrates such as aziridines are easily activated and hard to be synthesized, and these reactions often need Lewis-base sites to promote; Using new substrates such as aminoalcohols to react with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) is another way to synthesize oxazolidinones, but MOF catalysts used in this reaction has not been reported yet. Although synthesis of oxazolidinones by three-components reaction is simple and convenient, catalysts with high activity and selectivity are needed to deal with the complex reaction processes and by-products. Hence, the current research topics can focus on two points, one is constructed MOF catalysts with high stable that can tolerate harsh reaction conditions and alkaline environment, and the other one is designed efficiency catalysts that can catalyze these reactions under mild conditions in the absence of co-catalyst.
## 3. Synthesis of Cyclic Carbonates from \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) using MOFs Catalysts
Cyclic carbonates have many important applications in industry, they can directly use as solvent or electrolyte, and also can act as substrates or intermediates to synthesize polymer and medicine.[102–111] For example, propylene carbonate is a colorless and odorless liquid, it is widely applied as extractant of olefins and arenes, absorbent of \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\), and dispersant of water-soluble dyes or pigments; Vinylene carbonate is a new organic film forming additive and overcharge protection additive for lithium ions batteries, which can improve the capacity and cycle life of the battery.[112–114] Up to date, lots of noble-metal-free MOFs have been designed and applied in catalyzing synthesis of cyclic carbonates.[115–120] Although various substrates are
studied in reported literature, these reactions can be divided in three categories (Figure 6): cycloaddition of epoxides and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\), carboxylation cyclization of propargylic alcohols and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\), and cascade reaction.
## 3.1. Cycloaddition of Epoxides and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\)
Cycloaddition of epoxides and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) is an essential and widely studied method to synthesis of cyclic carbonates, and a large number of publications on noble-metal-free MOFs that have been published.[121–126] Hence, in order to avoid repetition with those existing reviews, we focus on developments in recent three years about noble-metal-free MOFs with new structures or methods to enhance the catalytic efficiency.
\(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) has an affinity toward nucleophiles and electron-donating reagents, such as \(\mathrm{Br}^{-}\), \(\mathrm{Cl}^{-}\), and \(\mathrm{I}^{-}\). These anions are often used in cycloaddition of epoxides and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) to accelerate the reaction, but they are toxic and complicate separation. Installing ionic liquids onto the frameworks by pre- or post-synthetic functionalization is a useful method to make this catalytic process fully heterogeneous. Gao's group fabricated a triazolium-based ionic MOF through post synthesis of MIL-101.[127] Owing to the Br ion was encapsulated within the pore, the obtained catalyst exhibited excellent performance for cycloaddition of epoxides and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) in the absence of co-catalyst.
Utilization of the synergistic effect between multiple active sites is an effective method to prepare catalysts. Zhong and co-workers designed a straightforward way to integrate multiple components into one MOF through mechanochemical synthesis.[128] ZIF-8 was selected as the precursor, after partially replacing the Zn ions with Co ions and enveloping ionic liquids (IL), catalyst \(\mathrm{IL}@\mathrm{ZIF}-8(\mathrm{Zn}/\mathrm{Co})\) with multiple sites was obtained. This catalyst exhibited a superior performance than that of the related individual components in cycloaddition of epoxides and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\), demonstrating that the synergistic effect is exist between cobalt ions and the IL in the ZIF-8 framework. Furthermore, the \(\mathrm{IL}@\mathrm{ZIF}-8(\mathrm{Zn}/\mathrm{Co})\) can maintain structural integrity during the catalytic cycles, and no appreciable reduction in product yield was observed for five cycles. This work provides a good example for fabricating multifunctional materials.
